How to Use This Code
Dataset Preparation:

Organize your dataset in the following structure:

data/
    train/
        class1/
            img1.jpg
            img2.jpg
            ...
        class2/
            img1.jpg
            img2.jpg
            ...
        ...
    test/
        class1/
            img1.jpg
            img2.jpg
            ...
        class2/
            img1.jpg
            img2.jpg
            ...
        ...
Dependencies:
Install the required packages:

pip install torch torchvision numpy scikit-learn tqdm pillow
Modify Parameters:

Adjust train_dir and test_dir to point to your dataset

Tune hyperparameters like batch_size, num_epochs, learning_rate, and margin as needed

Run the Code:
Simply execute the script to start training and evaluation.

Key Features
Triplet Loss Implementation: The code includes a proper implementation of triplet loss with margin.

ResNet Backbone: Uses ResNet50 as the base model with custom embedding layers.

Data Loading: Includes a custom dataset class that samples triplets (anchor, positive, negative).

Evaluation: Uses K-Nearest Neighbors on the embeddings to evaluate the model.

Reproducibility: Sets random seeds for consistent results.

This implementation provides a solid foundation for fine-tuning ResNet with triplet loss for tasks like face recognition, image retrieval, or any other metric learning application.
